{{JPExclusive}}
:''Not to be confused with [[Sakura Android (Enemy)|Sakura Android]].''
'''Droid Cat''' is a [[:Category:Rare Cats|Rare Cat]] that was added in [[Version 2.1 Update|Version 2.1]] and can be unlocked as an item drop during the [[Google Android Collaboration Event]]. [[True Form]] added in [[Version 3.5 Update|Version 3.5]] decreases cooldown.

{{Cat Info
|ID = 77
|rarity = RR
|name1 = Droid Cat
|name2 = Droid Cat Mk 2
|name3 = SpringDroid
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Droid Cat Mk 2''' at level 10.

Evolves into '''SpringDroid''' when obtained from the [[Droid Awakes!]] (may be dropped on the first stage but guaranteed on the 2nd stage) and is Level 20 or above.

==Strategy/Usage==
Droid Cat's cheap cost and [[Resistant|resistance]] against [[:Category:Metal Enemies|Metal]] enemies might seem promising, but sadly, its recharge time and slow movement speed make it too unreliable in maintaining your defense, being outclassed by [[Rope Jump Cat (Rare Cat)|Noodle Cats]] as an [[:Category:Anti-Metal Cats|anti-Metal]] [[:Category:Meatshield-class Cats|meatshield]]. It can't really tank high DPS Metal enemies from mid-game or end-game, such as [[Koronium]] or [[Sir Metal Seal]]. This makes him only worth getting for either collection purposes and/or the [[Cat Food]] reward.

==='''True Form'''===
SpringDroid is blessed with a decrease in cooldown. However, its cooldown is still very long. Like its previous forms, it still gets outclassed by Noodle Cats, who already perform badly against mid-game or late-game Metal enemies. Due to this, you will barely find any use in him once you progress through the game.

